module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.ExtensionOfSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleWire.UnitStalk
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Sections away from `V(I)` as homomorphisms out of a power of the ideal sheaf

Let `X` be a quasi-compact scheme, let `I` be a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals whose first power
`I • 𝒪_X` is of finite type, and let `F` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module. Writing `U` for the
open complement `X ∖ V(I)`, the canonical map
`colim_n Hom(I ^ n • 𝒪_X, F) ⟶ Γ(F, U)`
of `Stacks.LocalCohomology.canonicalMapToSections` is injective (Stacks tag 01PQ, proved in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.CanonicalSectionsInjective`). This file proves
that it is **surjective**, and hence bijective, as soon as `F` has no `I`-torsion: no nonzero
section of `F` over an affine chart is annihilated by the ideal of that chart.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.NoIdealTorsion`: `F` has no `I`-torsion.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.SmulExtends`: `SmulExtends I F s V x t` says that `t` is a section of
  `F` over `V` whose restriction to every open `W ≤ V` away from `V(I)` equals `x · s`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.extendableIdeal`: the ideal of those `x ∈ Γ(X, V)` for which `x · s`
  does extend to a section of `F` over `V`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_idealPow_smul_eq_zero_of_vanishing_on_complement`: on an affine
  chart, a section vanishing away from `V(I)` is annihilated by a single power of the ideal of
  the chart.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.eq_zero_of_vanishing_on_complement` and
  `Stacks.LocalCohomology.SmulExtends.unique`: with no `I`-torsion, a section over `V` is
  determined by its restriction to `V ∖ V(I)`; in particular an extension of `x · s` is unique.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_idealPow_le_extendableIdeal`: on an affine chart some power of
  the ideal of the chart is extendable.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.smulExtends_of_cover` and
  `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_smulExtends_of_locally`: extendability is a local condition, and
  local extensions glue.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_idealPowerMultiple_smulExtends`: one exponent `N` serves every
  open — for every open `V` and every section `x` of `I ^ N • 𝒪_X` over `V`, the product `x · s`
  extends over `V`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_idealPowerHom_of_section_of_noIdealTorsion`: every section of
  `F` over `X ∖ V(I)` is the value on the unit section of a morphism `I ^ N • 𝒪_X ⟶ F`.
* `Stacks.LocalCohomology.canonicalMapToSections_surjective_of_noIdealTorsion` and
  `Stacks.LocalCohomology.canonicalMapToSections_bijective_of_noIdealTorsion`: the canonical map
  is surjective, hence bijective.

## Implementation notes

The morphism `I ^ N • 𝒪_X ⟶ F` is built directly from its values on sections: a section `x` of
`I ^ N • 𝒪_X` over `V` is sent to the *unique* section of `F` over `V` which restricts to `x · s`
away from `V(I)`. Uniqueness is what makes the assignment additive, `Γ(X, V)`-linear and
compatible with restriction, so no coherence of the choices has to be checked separately; it is
also where the absence of `I`-torsion is used.

Existence of the extension is local and needs no torsion hypothesis. On an affine chart `W` where
`I(W)` is generated by a finite family `a`, the normal form
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_pow_smul_extends_on_affine` of `s` provides sections `m i` of `F`
over `W` restricting to `(a i) ^ k · s` away from `V(I)`, so every element of the ideal generated
by the `(a i) ^ k` is extendable; the pigeonhole bound
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSections.span_pow_le_span_image_pow` turns that into a power
of `I(W)`. The exponent produced this way depends on the chart, and a *single* exponent is
obtained from a finite affine cover: for an affine `W` inside a member `U` of the cover the ideal
`I(W)` is generated by the image of `I(U)`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal`, and extendability is inherited by
restriction, so the exponent of `U` already serves `W`.

The torsion hypothesis is **not** removed here; that is done, for a coherent `F` on a Noetherian
scheme, in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.LocalCohomology.SectionsOverOpenCoherent`, by the
replacement of `F` by `F' = I ^ m • F` for `m` large that the source performs: Artin–Rees
(`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_ideal_pow_smul_inf_eq`, tag 01YA) and the stabilization of the chain
of annihilator subsheaves
(`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_eventually_constant_quasicoherentSubobjects`, tag 01Y8) give
`F' ∩ F_n = 0` for every `n`, so `F'` has no `I`-torsion while `F'|_U = F|_U`. No tag is claimed
here: the hypothesis `NoIdealTorsion` is not part of tag 01YB.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01YB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01YB)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPower
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSections
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentBaseChange

universe u

namespace Stacks.LocalCohomology

open Stacks.Ample (unitModule)

noncomputable section

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Modules without `I`-torsion -/

/-- `F` has no `I`-torsion: on every affine chart, a section annihilated by the whole ideal
there is zero. This is the sheaf form of the hypothesis `I x = 0 → x = 0` of Stacks tag 01PM. -/
public def NoIdealTorsion (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) : Prop :=
  ∀ (U : X.affineOpens) (y : Γ(F, (U : X.Opens))),
    (∀ b ∈ I.ideal U, b • y = 0) → y = 0

/-- Some power of the ideal generated by a finite family lies in the ideal generated by the
`k`-th powers of its members, for `1 ≤ k`. -/
private theorem exists_span_pow_le_powerSpan {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {ι : Type*} [Finite ι]
    (a : ι → A) (k : ℕ) (hk : 1 ≤ k) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, Ideal.span (Set.range a) ^ N ≤ powerSpan a k := by
  classical
  have := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  exact ⟨_, idealPow_le_powerSpan a k hk (Finset.univ.image a) (by simp)⟩

/-- Every point of an open set lies in an affine open contained in it. -/
private theorem exists_affineOpen_le_of_mem {U : X.Opens} {y : X} (hy : y ∈ U) :
    ∃ W : X.affineOpens, y ∈ (W : X.Opens) ∧ (W : X.Opens) ≤ U := by
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨W, hW, rfl⟩, hyW, hWU⟩ := X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hy U.2
  exact ⟨⟨W, hW⟩, hyW, hWU⟩

/-- A section of a quasi-coherent module over an affine chart whose restriction to every open
away from `V(I)` vanishes is annihilated by a single power of the ideal of that chart.

The ideal of the chart is generated by a finite family, the basic opens of whose members cover
the part of the chart away from `V(I)`; each generator therefore annihilates the section after
raising it to some power, and the pigeonhole bound
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSections.span_pow_le_span_image_pow` turns a uniform such
power into a power of the ideal itself. -/
@[ega "I 1.4.1" "partial"]
public lemma exists_idealPow_smul_eq_zero_of_vanishing_on_complement
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    [((idealPowerMultiple I 1 (unitModule X)).toModules).IsFiniteType]
    (U : X.affineOpens) (t : Γ(F, (U : X.Opens)))
    (ht : ∀ (W : X.Opens) (hWU : W ≤ (U : X.Opens)), W ≤ idealComplement I →
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op t = 0) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ b ∈ (I.ideal U ^ N : Ideal Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))), b • t = 0 := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨ι, hι, a, hspan⟩ := exists_finite_generating_family I U
  have hfin : Fintype ι := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  have hamem : ∀ i, a i ∈ I.ideal U := fun i => hspan ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨i, rfl⟩
  have hzero : ∀ i, F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le (a i))).op t = 0 := fun i =>
    ht (X.basicOpen (a i)) (X.basicOpen_le (a i))
      (basicOpen_le_idealComplement I U (hamem i))
  choose k hk using fun i =>
    exists_pow_smul_eq_zero_of_restrict_eq_zero F U.2 (a i) t (hzero i)
  set K := max (Finset.univ.sup k) 1 with hKdef
  have hK1 : 1 ≤ K := le_max_right _ 1
  have hKall : ∀ i, a i ^ K • t = 0 := by
    intro i
    have hle : k i ≤ K :=
      le_trans (Finset.le_sup (Finset.mem_univ i)) (le_max_left _ 1)
    rw [← Nat.sub_add_cancel hle, pow_add, mul_smul, hk i, smul_zero]
  have hps := smul_eq_zero_of_pow_smul_eq_zero a K t hKall
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := exists_span_pow_le_powerSpan a K hK1
  exact ⟨N, fun b hb => hps b (hN (hspan ▸ hb))⟩

/-- A section of a quasi-coherent module without `I`-torsion whose restriction to every open
away from `V(I)` vanishes is itself zero.

This is the uniqueness half of the extension problem: a section over an open `V` is determined
by its restriction to `V ∖ V(I)`. -/
public lemma eq_zero_of_vanishing_on_complement
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    [((idealPowerMultiple I 1 (unitModule X)).toModules).IsFiniteType]
    (hTF : NoIdealTorsion I F) (V : X.Opens) (t : Γ(F, V))
    (ht : ∀ (W : X.Opens) (hWV : W ≤ V), W ≤ idealComplement I →
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op t = 0) :
    t = 0 := by
  classical
  refine TopCat.Presheaf.IsSheaf.section_ext F.isSheaf (U := op V) (t := 0) ?_
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨Wa, hyW, hWle⟩ := exists_affineOpen_le_of_mem hy
  refine ⟨(Wa : X.Opens), hWle, hyW, ?_⟩
  rw [map_zero]
  set t' : Γ(F, (Wa : X.Opens)) := F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWle).op t with ht'def
  have hvan : ∀ (W' : X.Opens) (hW' : W' ≤ (Wa : X.Opens)), W' ≤ idealComplement I →
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hW').op t' = 0 := by
    intro W' hW' hW'c
    rw [ht'def, map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]
    exact ht W' (hW'.trans hWle) hW'c
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ :=
    exists_idealPow_smul_eq_zero_of_vanishing_on_complement I F Wa t' hvan
  exact eq_zero_of_idealPow_smul_eq_zero (I.ideal Wa) (hTF Wa) N t' hN

/-! ### The extension predicate and the ideal of extendable sections -/

/-- `SmulExtends I F s V x t` says that `t` is a section of `F` over `V` whose restriction to
every open `W ≤ V` disjoint from `V(I)` is `x · s`.

This is the extension problem solved pointwise in the index of the direct system: a morphism
`I ^ n • 𝒪_X ⟶ F` whose value on the unit section is `s` is exactly a choice of such a `t` for
every open and every section of `I ^ n • 𝒪_X` there. -/
public def SmulExtends (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules)
    (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) (V : X.Opens) (x : Γ(X, V)) (t : Γ(F, V)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (W : X.Opens) (hWV : W ≤ V) (hWc : W ≤ idealComplement I),
    F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op t =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op x • F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWc).op s

/-- The zero section extends the zero multiple of `s`. -/
public lemma smulExtends_zero (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules)
    (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) (V : X.Opens) :
    SmulExtends I F s V 0 0 := by
  intro W hWV _
  rw [map_zero, map_zero, zero_smul]

/-- Extensions add. -/
public lemma SmulExtends.add {I : X.IdealSheafData} {F : X.Modules}
    {s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)} {V : X.Opens} {x y : Γ(X, V)} {t t' : Γ(F, V)}
    (h : SmulExtends I F s V x t) (h' : SmulExtends I F s V y t') :
    SmulExtends I F s V (x + y) (t + t') := by
  intro W hWV hWc
  rw [map_add, map_add, h W hWV hWc, h' W hWV hWc, add_smul]

/-- Extensions are compatible with the action of the structure sheaf. -/
public lemma SmulExtends.smul {I : X.IdealSheafData} {F : X.Modules}
    {s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)} {V : X.Opens} {x : Γ(X, V)} {t : Γ(F, V)}
    (h : SmulExtends I F s V x t) (c : Γ(X, V)) :
    SmulExtends I F s V (c • x) (c • t) := by
  intro W hWV hWc
  have hm : (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op).hom (c • x) =
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op).hom c * (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op).hom x :=
    map_mul _ c x
  rw [F.map_smul, h W hWV hWc, smul_smul, hm]

/-- Extensions restrict. -/
public lemma SmulExtends.restrict {I : X.IdealSheafData} {F : X.Modules}
    {s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)} {V : X.Opens} {x : Γ(X, V)} {t : Γ(F, V)}
    (h : SmulExtends I F s V x t) {V' : X.Opens} (hV' : V' ≤ V) :
    SmulExtends I F s V' (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV').op x)
      (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV').op t) := by
  intro W hWV' hWc
  rw [map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE, structureSheaf_map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]
  exact h W (hWV'.trans hV') hWc

/-- **Uniqueness of the extension.** If `F` has no `I`-torsion, a section of `F` over `V` is
determined by its restriction to the part of `V` away from `V(I)`. -/
public lemma SmulExtends.unique {I : X.IdealSheafData} {F : X.Modules} [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    [((idealPowerMultiple I 1 (unitModule X)).toModules).IsFiniteType]
    (hTF : NoIdealTorsion I F) {s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)} {V : X.Opens} {x : Γ(X, V)}
    {t t' : Γ(F, V)} (h : SmulExtends I F s V x t) (h' : SmulExtends I F s V x t') :
    t = t' := by
  refine sub_eq_zero.mp
    (eq_zero_of_vanishing_on_complement I F hTF V (t - t') fun W hWV hWc => ?_)
  rw [map_sub, h W hWV hWc, h' W hWV hWc, sub_self]

/-- The ideal of those sections of the structure sheaf over `V` whose product with `s` extends
to a section of `F` over `V`. -/
public def extendableIdeal (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules)
    (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) (V : X.Opens) : Ideal Γ(X, V) where
  carrier := {x | ∃ t, SmulExtends I F s V x t}
  zero_mem' := ⟨0, smulExtends_zero I F s V⟩
  add_mem' := fun ⟨t, ht⟩ ⟨t', ht'⟩ => ⟨t + t', ht.add ht'⟩
  smul_mem' := fun c _ ⟨t, ht⟩ => ⟨c • t, ht.smul c⟩

/-- Membership in `extendableIdeal` unfolded. -/
public lemma mem_extendableIdeal {I : X.IdealSheafData} {F : X.Modules}
    {s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)} {V : X.Opens} {x : Γ(X, V)} :
    x ∈ extendableIdeal I F s V ↔ ∃ t, SmulExtends I F s V x t :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- Extendability is inherited by restriction to a smaller open. -/
public lemma map_extendableIdeal_le (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules)
    (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) {V W : X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) :
    (extendableIdeal I F s V).map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op).hom ≤
      extendableIdeal I F s W :=
  Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun _ ⟨t, ht⟩ => ⟨F.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op t, ht.restrict h⟩

/-- **A power of the ideal of a chart is extendable.** On an affine chart, a section of a
quasi-coherent module over `X ∖ V(I)` has the property that its product with any element of a
high enough power of the ideal of the chart extends to a section over the whole chart.

The exponent is the pigeonhole exponent of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealPowerSections.span_pow_le_span_image_pow` for the normal form of
`s` on the chart, which is `Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_pow_smul_extends_on_affine`. -/
public lemma exists_idealPow_le_extendableIdeal (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules)
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] [((idealPowerMultiple I 1 (unitModule X)).toModules).IsFiniteType]
    (U : X.affineOpens) (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, (I.ideal U ^ N : Ideal Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))) ≤
      extendableIdeal I F s (U : X.Opens) := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨ι, hι, a, hspan⟩ := exists_finite_generating_family I U
  have hfin : Fintype ι := Fintype.ofFinite ι
  obtain ⟨k, m, hm⟩ := exists_pow_smul_extends_on_affine I F U a hspan s
  set k' := max k 1
  have hk1 : 1 ≤ k' := le_max_right _ 1
  have hkk : k ≤ k' := le_max_left _ 1
  have hmem : ∀ i, a i ^ k' ∈ extendableIdeal I F s (U : X.Opens) := by
    intro i
    refine ⟨a i ^ (k' - k) • m i, fun W hWU hWc => ?_⟩
    have hWinf : W ≤ (U : X.Opens) ⊓ idealComplement I := le_inf hWU hWc
    have hmW : F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op (m i) =
        (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op (a i)) ^ k •
          F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWc).op s := by
      have h1 := congrArg (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWinf).op) (hm i)
      rwa [map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE, F.map_smul, map_pow,
        structureSheaf_map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE, map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE] at h1
    rw [F.map_smul, map_pow, hmW, map_pow, smul_smul, ← pow_add,
      Nat.sub_add_cancel hkk]
  have hspanle : powerSpan a k' ≤ extendableIdeal I F s (U : X.Opens) := by
    rw [powerSpan]
    refine Ideal.span_le.mpr ?_
    rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨i, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    exact hmem i
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := exists_span_pow_le_powerSpan a k' hk1
  exact ⟨N, hspan ▸ hN.trans hspanle⟩

/-! ### Extendability is local -/

/-- Being an extension of `x · s` is a local condition on the open. -/
public lemma smulExtends_of_cover {I : X.IdealSheafData} {F : X.Modules}
    {s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)} {V : X.Opens} {x : Γ(X, V)} {t : Γ(F, V)}
    {ι : Type*} (W : ι → X.Opens) (hWV : ∀ p, W p ≤ V) (hcov : V ≤ ⨆ p, W p)
    (h : ∀ p, SmulExtends I F s (W p) (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hWV p)).op x)
      (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hWV p)).op t)) :
    SmulExtends I F s V x t := by
  intro V₀ hV₀V hV₀c
  refine TopCat.Presheaf.IsSheaf.section_ext F.isSheaf (U := op V₀) ?_
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨p, hyp⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.1 (hcov (hV₀V hy))
  have hZV₀ : V₀ ⊓ W p ≤ V₀ := inf_le_left
  have hZW : V₀ ⊓ W p ≤ W p := inf_le_right
  have hZc : V₀ ⊓ W p ≤ idealComplement I := hZV₀.trans hV₀c
  refine ⟨V₀ ⊓ W p, hZV₀, ⟨hy, hyp⟩, ?_⟩
  have hleft : F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZV₀).op (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV₀V).op t) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hZV₀.trans hV₀V)).op x •
        F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hZc).op s := by
    rw [map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]
    have h1 := h p (V₀ ⊓ W p) hZW hZc
    rwa [map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE, structureSheaf_map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE] at h1
  rw [hleft, F.map_smul, map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE,
    structureSheaf_map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]

/-- **Local extensions glue.** If `x · s` extends to a section of `F` near every point of `V`,
then it extends to a section over `V`.

The local extensions agree on overlaps because an extension is unique, by
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.SmulExtends.unique`, and the sheaf condition glues them. -/
public lemma exists_smulExtends_of_locally {I : X.IdealSheafData} {F : X.Modules}
    [F.IsQuasicoherent] [((idealPowerMultiple I 1 (unitModule X)).toModules).IsFiniteType]
    (hTF : NoIdealTorsion I F) {s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)} (V : X.Opens) (x : Γ(X, V))
    (h : ∀ y ∈ V, ∃ (W : X.Opens) (hWV : W ≤ V), y ∈ W ∧
      ∃ t, SmulExtends I F s W (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op x) t) :
    ∃ t, SmulExtends I F s V x t := by
  classical
  choose W hWV hyW t ht using h
  let ι := { y : X // y ∈ V }
  let W' : ι → X.Opens := fun p => W p.1 p.2
  let t' : ∀ p : ι, Γ(F, W' p) := fun p => t p.1 p.2
  have hW'V : ∀ p : ι, W' p ≤ V := fun p => hWV p.1 p.2
  have ht' : ∀ p : ι, SmulExtends I F s (W' p)
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hW'V p)).op x) (t' p) := fun p => ht p.1 p.2
  have hcov : V ≤ ⨆ p : ι, W' p := fun y hy =>
    TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, hyW y hy⟩
  have hcpt : TopCat.Presheaf.IsCompatible F.presheaf W' t' := by
    intro p q
    have hlp : W' p ⊓ W' q ≤ W' p := inf_le_left
    have hlq : W' p ⊓ W' q ≤ W' q := inf_le_right
    change F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hlp).op (t' p) =
      F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hlq).op (t' q)
    have hp := (ht' p).restrict hlp
    have hq := (ht' q).restrict hlq
    rw [structureSheaf_map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE] at hp hq
    refine SmulExtends.unique hTF hp ?_
    convert hq using 2
  obtain ⟨s₀, hs₀, -⟩ :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.IsSheaf.isSheafUniqueGluing F.isSheaf W' t' hcpt
  refine ⟨F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hcov).op s₀, ?_⟩
  refine smulExtends_of_cover W' hW'V hcov fun p => ?_
  have hres : F.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hW'V p)).op
      (F.presheaf.map (homOfLE hcov).op s₀) = t' p := by
    rw [map_homOfLE_map_homOfLE]
    exact hs₀ p
  rw [hres]
  exact ht' p

/-! ### One exponent for the whole scheme -/

/-- **One exponent serves every open.** On a quasi-compact scheme, for a quasi-coherent module
without `I`-torsion and a finite-type ideal sheaf, there is one exponent `N` such that for every
open `V` and every section `x` of `I ^ N • 𝒪_X` over `V`, the product `x · s` extends to a
section of `F` over `V`.

The exponent is the supremum of the chart exponents of
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_idealPow_le_extendableIdeal` over a finite affine cover; it
serves an arbitrary affine open `W` inside a member `U` of the cover because the ideal of `W` is
generated by the image of the ideal of `U`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal`, and extendability is inherited by
restriction. -/
public lemma exists_idealPowerMultiple_smulExtends
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [CompactSpace X] [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    [((idealPowerMultiple I 1 (unitModule X)).toModules).IsFiniteType]
    (hTF : NoIdealTorsion I F) (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) :
    ∃ N : ℕ, ∀ (V : X.Opens) (x : Γ(X, V)),
      x ∈ (idealPowerMultiple I N (unitModule X)).toSubmodule.obj (op V) →
      ∃ t, SmulExtends I F s V x t := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨n, Uc, hAffine, hcover⟩ := exists_fin_affineOpen_cover (X := X)
  let Ua : Fin n → X.affineOpens := fun j => ⟨Uc j, hAffine j⟩
  choose Nj hNj using fun j => exists_idealPow_le_extendableIdeal I F (Ua j) s
  refine ⟨Finset.univ.sup Nj, fun V x hx => ?_⟩
  refine exists_smulExtends_of_locally hTF V x fun y hy => ?_
  have hytop : y ∈ (⊤ : X.Opens) := trivial
  rw [← hcover] at hytop
  obtain ⟨j, hyj⟩ := TopologicalSpace.Opens.mem_iSup.1 hytop
  obtain ⟨Wa, hyW, hWsub⟩ := exists_affineOpen_le_of_mem (show y ∈ V ⊓ Uc j from ⟨hy, hyj⟩)
  have hWV : (Wa : X.Opens) ≤ V := hWsub.trans inf_le_left
  have hWU : Wa ≤ Ua j := hWsub.trans inf_le_right
  refine ⟨(Wa : X.Opens), hWV, hyW, ?_⟩
  have hxW : X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWV).op x ∈
      (I.ideal Wa ^ Finset.univ.sup Nj : Ideal Γ(X, (Wa : X.Opens))) := by
    have h0 := (idealPowerMultiple I (Finset.univ.sup Nj) (unitModule X)).toSubmodule.map
      (homOfLE hWV).op hx
    rwa [idealPowerMultiple_obj_affine I (Finset.univ.sup Nj) Wa] at h0
  have hchain : (I.ideal Wa ^ Finset.univ.sup Nj : Ideal Γ(X, (Wa : X.Opens))) ≤
      extendableIdeal I F s (Wa : X.Opens) := by
    have hpow : (I.ideal Wa ^ Finset.univ.sup Nj : Ideal Γ(X, (Wa : X.Opens))) =
        (I.ideal (Ua j) ^ Finset.univ.sup Nj :
            Ideal Γ(X, ((Ua j : X.affineOpens) : X.Opens))).map
          (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op).hom := by
      rw [Ideal.map_pow, I.map_ideal hWU]
    rw [hpow]
    refine le_trans (Ideal.map_mono ?_) (map_extendableIdeal_le I F s hWU)
    exact le_trans (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (Finset.le_sup (Finset.mem_univ j))) (hNj j)
  exact hchain hxW

/-! ### The morphism out of a power of the ideal sheaf -/

/-- The object of the ideal-power system at `n` is the ideal-power subsheaf itself. -/
public lemma idealPowerSystem_obj (I : X.IdealSheafData) (M : X.Modules) (n : ℕ) :
    (idealPowerSystem I M).obj (op n) = (idealPowerMultiple I n M).toModules :=
  rfl

/-- **The extension problem is solvable when `F` has no `I`-torsion.** On a quasi-compact scheme,
for a finite-type ideal sheaf `I` and a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `F` with no `I`-torsion,
every section of `F` over `X ∖ V(I)` is the value on the unit section of a morphism
`I ^ N • 𝒪_X ⟶ F`.

The morphism sends a section `x` of `I ^ N • 𝒪_X` over an open `V` to the unique section of `F`
over `V` restricting to `x · s` away from `V(I)`; existence is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.exists_idealPowerMultiple_smulExtends` and uniqueness is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.SmulExtends.unique`, and uniqueness is also what makes the assignment
additive, linear and compatible with restriction. -/
public theorem exists_idealPowerHom_of_section_of_noIdealTorsion
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [CompactSpace X] [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    [((idealPowerMultiple I 1 (unitModule X)).toModules).IsFiniteType]
    (hTF : NoIdealTorsion I F) (s : Γ(F, idealComplement I)) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (φ : (idealPowerSystem I (unitModule X)).obj (op N) ⟶ F),
      (φ.val.app (op (idealComplement I))).hom
        (complementUnitLift I N (idealComplement I) le_rfl) = s := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨N, hN⟩ := exists_idealPowerMultiple_smulExtends I F hTF s
  have hex : ∀ (V : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ)
      (z : ↥((idealPowerMultiple I N (unitModule X)).toSubmodule.obj V)),
      ∃ t : Γ(F, V.unop), SmulExtends I F s V.unop z.1 t := fun V z => hN V.unop z.1 z.2
  choose tf htf using hex
  have huniq : ∀ (V : X.Opens) (x : Γ(X, V)) (t t' : Γ(F, V)),
      SmulExtends I F s V x t → SmulExtends I F s V x t' → t = t' :=
    fun _ _ _ _ h h' => SmulExtends.unique hTF h h'
  let appV : ∀ V : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ,
      ((idealPowerMultiple I N (unitModule X)).toModules).val.obj V ⟶ F.val.obj V :=
    fun V => ModuleCat.ofHom
      { toFun := tf V
        map_add' := fun z w =>
          huniq V.unop _ _ _ (htf V (z + w)) ((htf V z).add (htf V w))
        map_smul' := fun c z =>
          huniq V.unop _ _ _ (htf V (c • z)) ((htf V z).smul c) }
  let φ : (idealPowerSystem I (unitModule X)).obj (op N) ⟶ F :=
    ⟨{ app := appV
       naturality := by
         intro V W f
         ext z
         have hres := (htf V z).restrict f.unop.le
         rw [Subsingleton.elim (homOfLE f.unop.le).op f] at hres
         exact huniq W.unop _ _ _ (htf W _) hres }⟩
  refine ⟨N, φ, ?_⟩
  have h := htf (op (idealComplement I))
    (complementUnitLift I N (idealComplement I) le_rfl)
    (idealComplement I) le_rfl le_rfl
  change tf (op (idealComplement I))
    (complementUnitLift I N (idealComplement I) le_rfl) = s
  simpa [complementUnitLift] using h

/-! ### Surjectivity and bijectivity of the canonical map -/

/-- **Surjectivity of the canonical map for a module without `I`-torsion.** On a quasi-compact
scheme, for a finite-type quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals `I` and a quasi-coherent module `F` with
no `I`-torsion, the canonical map
`colim_n Hom(I ^ n • 𝒪_X, F) → Γ(F, X ∖ V(I))`
is surjective. -/
public theorem canonicalMapToSections_surjective_of_noIdealTorsion
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [CompactSpace X] [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    [((idealPowerMultiple I 1 (unitModule X)).toModules).IsFiniteType]
    (hTF : NoIdealTorsion I F) :
    Function.Surjective (canonicalMapToSections I F).1 := by
  rw [canonicalMapToSections_surjective_iff]
  exact exists_idealPowerHom_of_section_of_noIdealTorsion I F hTF

/-- **The canonical map is a bijection for a module without `I`-torsion.** This is the
torsion-free case of the `sectionsOverOpen` clause of Stacks tag 01YB: injectivity is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.canonicalMapToSections_injective` (tag 01PQ) and surjectivity is
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.canonicalMapToSections_surjective_of_noIdealTorsion`.

No Noetherian hypothesis is needed: quasi-compactness of `X`, finite type of the ideal sheaf and
quasi-coherence of `F` suffice once `F` has no `I`-torsion. The general case of tag 01YB is
reduced to this one by replacing `F` with `I ^ m • F` for `m` large, which requires both the
Artin–Rees lemma and the stabilization of the chain of annihilator subsheaves, hence `X`
Noetherian and `F` coherent. -/
public theorem canonicalMapToSections_bijective_of_noIdealTorsion
    (I : X.IdealSheafData) (F : X.Modules) [CompactSpace X] [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    [((idealPowerMultiple I 1 (unitModule X)).toModules).IsFiniteType]
    (hTF : NoIdealTorsion I F) :
    Function.Bijective (canonicalMapToSections I F).1 :=
  ⟨canonicalMapToSections_injective I F,
    canonicalMapToSections_surjective_of_noIdealTorsion I F hTF⟩

end

